WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:04.867
Found a winner? Take it with you. Into CAD, into Excel, or into a client
report.

2
00:00:05.817 --> 00:00:08.107
Episode five. Lookup and exports.

3
00:00:09.057 --> 00:00:16.375
Reports and Exports has everything you'd share: a printable feasibility
report, a shareable web page, and a site plan sheet.

4
00:00:17.275 --> 00:00:25.895
For designers: a DXF for AutoCAD, Rhino, or Revit, an OBJ 3D model,
and GeoJSON for GIS.

5
00:00:26.795 --> 00:00:31.213
For the numbers people: an Excel pro forma with every year and every
assumption.

6
00:00:32.113 --> 00:00:36.553
Plus Street View and Google Maps links, so you can see the site before
you drive out.

7
00:00:37.453 --> 00:00:42.015
Already have a property in mind? Open Site Lookup, and type any U.S.
address.

8
00:00:42.915 --> 00:00:46.474
You get the same snapshot and full analysis, for that one parcel.

9
00:00:47.374 --> 00:00:56.768
One last thing. SiteVerge is a first screen, not a final answer. Always
verify zoning, title, and costs with the city and licensed professionals.

10
00:00:57.818 --> 00:01:00.021
That's SiteVerge. Go find your next site.

